;;; An obligation a node is told about that root was not — M1e2 **W26**,
;;; register row `W26/oblig-derived-activator` (`corpus/wrong_answers.toml`),
;;; banked by S1e2.2.25 (2026-11-05) for the inventory of 2026-11-05's W-15
;;; (Q-M1e.11), which had no witness, and filed `open`, deferred to M1f's
;;; S1f.10.6 on the user's ruling of that day (Q-M1e2.16 (5)). Its control is
;;; `oblig-derived-activator-declared.ein`, which states the activator.
;;;
;;; ── What this program is ───────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; `std.algebra`'s `total-owed` over `likes`, stated, and over `drinks`,
;;; whose activator `(total-owed drinks is-a)` the rule `arm` derives from any
;;; `likes` fact: an obligation's activator that only a commitment derives.
;;;
;;; ── The answer, by hand ────────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; Ann owes a Food and, once she likes one, a Drink. `{(likes Ann Soup),
;;; (drinks Ann Tea)}` pays both debts, so R holds it, as the control's R is
;;; that one state.
;;;
;;; ── What the engine answers ────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; The obligations rung builds H from the debts root owes, so H is
;;; `{(likes Ann Soup)}`: the facts that would discharge the debt a node is
;;; told about are never candidates. The one node, `{(likes Ann Soup)}`, owes
;;; `drinks`, and R is empty, every alive node owing (`ein solve FILE` and
;;; `ein oracle FILE` at `94c75204`, release and debug alike). The static
;;; check flags the program (`total-owed`'s activator relation is one a
;;; commitment can change), and Q-M1e2.10's decline, which reads an
;;; obligation's guard over D, does not see a plan root does not have. What
;;; the search should do here is Q-M1e.11, M1f S1f.10.6's.

(import std.algebra :symbols (total-owed))
(relation is-a   T T :why "{?1} is a {?2}")
(relation likes  Person Food :why "{?1} likes {?2}")
(relation drinks Person Drink :why "{?1} drinks {?2}")
(is-a Ann Person) (is-a Soup Food) (is-a Tea Drink)
(total-owed likes is-a)
(rule arm () :match (likes ?p ?f) :assert (total-owed drinks is-a) :why "{?p} likes {?f}, which switches on the debt that every Person drinks a Drink")
(solve :no-hypothesis (is-a))
